Empty for the same reason stdout.log is: bench.py writes nothing to stderr on
any path, and this run's driver stream was not redirected to a file. No stderr
is reconstructed.

Child-process stderr IS captured, per row, in logs/*.err -- including every
failure: the 32 Macaulay2 std::bad_alloc aborts and the 4 Singular timeouts are
there in full, and are the failures that matter for this run.
